{
  "_comment": "The single source of truth for MonitorCLT signals. Consolidates the scattered configs (score weights, signals_catalog, env_sources) into one prioritizable list. Each signal carries: family, dimension (the five-score bucket), arbitrage_class (the SEVEN ways we make money from information), source, availability, cadence, and the four scoring attributes value/reliability/effort/legality. prioritize.py ranks 'what to build next' AND reports coverage by arbitrage_class -- which is more strategically useful than counting signals. This is a seed; the point is prioritization, not completeness. availability: wired|derived|free-add|env-free|sos-paid|rod-browser|court-browser|mls-paid|not-obtainable. status: built|config-ready|not-started. value/reliability/effort are 1-5. legality: ok|sensitive.",

  "_arbitrage_comment": "The seven arbitrages are the top-level taxonomy: the 150 lists are the raw material, these are the product. Every signal earns money one of these ways. Reporting coverage by class tells us where we're deep (distress) and thin (relationship), which is the strategic question. distress=owner/property needs a solution. timing=we see it earlier. complexity=a solvable problem others avoid. development=higher-and-better use. relationship=worth more to a specific buyer. information=records combine to reveal the invisible. catalyst=a known event is approaching.",
  "arbitrage_classes": ["distress", "timing", "complexity", "development", "relationship", "information", "catalyst", "meta"],

